    "https://dyouville-university.prismhr-hire.com/job/1047201/school-of-health-professions-physical-therapy-faculty-neurologic-pt": {
      "title": "School of Health Professions- Physical Therapy Faculty (Neurologic PT) @ D'Youville University",
      "description": "School of Health Professions- Physical Therapy Faculty (Neurologic PT) @ D'Youville University Share: School of Health Professions- Physical Therapy Faculty (Neurologic PT) Buffalo, NY $70,000 ‒ $75,000 Annually Apply for this position Back to Jobs D’Youville University invites applications for a full-time Assistant or Associate Professor in the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program, with specialization in neurologic physical therapy and interest in contributing to the clinical education curriculum. This faculty position will support teaching, curriculum development, and shared governance within a CAPTE-accredited program. Faculty rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Faculty in the Physical Therapy Department contribute to the development, implementation, and evaluation of the DPT curriculum within a collaborative, shared-governance model. Responsibilities: Teaching in the neurologic area of practice and contributing to the broader curriculum as appropriate Assisting the Director of Clinical Education in delivering high-quality clinical education experiences and applying best practices in clinical teaching Developing, updating, and evaluating course materials and participating in assessment of student learning Supporting student success through advising, mentorship, and regular office hours Engaging with clinical partners, the Simulation Center, and the Thrive Rehabilitation Center to enhance experiential learning Participating in department, school, and university committees, including Faculty Senate representation Contributing to scholarship consistent with the Boyer Model, including teaching, integration, application, discovery, and engagement Qualifications: Education: Eligible for licensure as a Physical Therapist in New York State Earned Doctor of Physical Therapy degree (DPT) plus advanced specialty certification or a research/academic doctorate (NCS, PhD, EdD, DSc, etc.) Experience: Minimum of five years of clinical experience, including student supervision Demonstrated excellence in interpersonal, written, and verbal communication Skills & Abilities: Commitment to ongoing professional development and maintaining currency in neurologic practice and clinical education principles Ability to create culturally responsive, inclusive learning environments Skill in collaborative teamwork and navigating diverse perspectives productively Experience using innovative, evidence-based teaching and learning strategies Ability to support accreditation processes and continuous program improvement efforts Applicants should submit: A letter of interest describing their qualifications, experience, and alignment with the position (Assistant or Associate rank) A current curriculum vitae including education, clinical and teaching experience, scholarship, licensure, and certifications Candidates invited for an interview will be asked to provide with contact information for five professional references including name, email and telephone number and description of professional relationship. Work Remotely - No Work Location: Buffalo, NY Job Type: Full Time, Exempt Pay: $70,000.00 - $75,000.00 Annually Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Faculty rank will be commensurate with education and qualifications. About D'Youville University: Shaping the Future of Education at D'Youville University D’Youville University, a nationally ranked private university in Buffalo, New York, is transforming lives through a unique blend of academics and holistic development. Committed to promoting a health mind, body, and spirit, D’Youville empowers individuals to realize their potential, thrive in their careers, and make meaningful contributions to society. A Dynamic and Purpose-Driven Community Located on Buffalo’s vibrant West Side, just blocks from a bustling downtown, D’Youville University is deeply embedded in an energetic, diverse urban landscape. Under the visionary leadership of President Lorrie Clemo, the university is undergoing an exciting evolution, with innovative initiatives designed to meet societal needs, elevate student experiences, expand career readiness, and solidify our role as a leader in 21st-century education. A Place for Growth and Innovation D’Youville University offers education across health sciences and business, with a range of degree levels, advanced certificates, accelerated paths, and community-engaged learning experiences. Our dedication to preparing students for successful careers is showcased in our national ranking for social mobility making us the top private university in the City of Buffalo. Why Work with Us? As a D’Youville University Saint, you’ll be joining a collaborative, innovation-driven community committed to academic excellence, social responsibility, and transformative growth. When you join our team, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a university making a real difference—for our students, our community, and our world. Explore the possibilities at dyu.edu . All job offers are contingent upon legal authorization to work in New York State as determined by the NYS Department of Labor. Apply for this position Get Updates Are you interested in hearing about new opportunities at D'Youville University? Enter your email address to get a weekly email when new positions are posted. send Powered by HiringThing © 2026\n\t\t\t\t| Privacy Policy Admin Login | Subscribe via RSS"
    },
    "https://dyouville-university.prismhr-hire.com/job/1047434/school-of-pharmacy-faculty-pharmacy-practice-ambulatory-care": {
      "title": "School of Pharmacy",
      "description": "School of Pharmacy - Faculty, Pharmacy Practice (Ambulatory Care) @ D'Youville University Share: School of Pharmacy - Faculty, Pharmacy Practice (Ambulatory Care) Buffalo, NY $100,000 ‒ $120,000 Annually Apply for this position Back to Jobs The primary responsibility of this faculty member is to coordinate and deliver instruction throughout the School’s pharmacotherapeutics and pharmacy practice curriculum with a focus on ambulatory care and chronic disease state management in both the traditional and online pathways. Additional teaching assignments may be designated at the discretion of the Chair of Pharmacy Practice. The faculty member will maintain an active ambulatory care clinical practice that supports direct patient care, population health initiatives, and interprofessional collaboration. The individual will serve as a preceptor for Doctor of Pharmacy students in both Introductory Pharmacy Practice Experiences (IPPEs) and Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiences (APPEs), fostering the development of clinical reasoning, patient-centered care, and professional competencies. Responsibilities: Teaching Coordinate and deliver didactic, laboratory, and experiential instruction within the Pharm.D. curriculum, with emphasis on ambulatory care, population health, and evidence-based pharmacotherapy. Develop, assess, and continuously improve course materials in alignment with programmatic outcomes and ACPE standards. Facilitate active learning strategies and innovative educational approaches in both face-to-face and online learning environments. Serve as a faculty advisor and mentor to Pharm.D. students. Clinical Practice and Precepting Maintain an active ambulatory care clinical practice that advances patient care and supports the mission of the School and affiliated healthcare partners. Provide direct patient care services such as comprehensive medication management, chronic disease management, preventive care, and transitions of care. Precept and mentor pharmacy students during IPPE and APPE rotations. Participate in interprofessional healthcare teams and collaborative practice initiatives. Scholarship Engage in scholarly activities that contribute to the advancement of pharmacy practice, pharmacy education, and/or ambulatory care. Disseminate scholarly work through presentations, publications, grant activities, or other recognized scholarly endeavors. Maintain a scholarly agenda consistent with expectations for appointment renewal and promotion. Service Participate in School, University, and departmental committee assignments as required. Contribute to professional organizations and pharmacy practice initiatives at the local, state, or national level. Engage in community outreach and service activities consistent with the mission and values of D’Youville University. Support accreditation, assessment, recruitment, and other strategic initiatives of the School of Pharmacy. Qualifications Education: Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE-accredited program. Completion of an ASHP-accredited PGY1 Pharmacy Residency. Completion of a PGY2 Ambulatory Care Residency preferred. Eligibility for pharmacist licensure in New York State. Board certification (e.g., BCACP) preferred. Experience: Demonstrated experience in ambulatory care practice, including chronic disease state management, medication optimization, patient education, and collaborative care. Skills & Abilities: Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to work collaboratively with healthcare professionals, faculty, staff, and students. Proficiency with electronic health records, learning management systems, and other educational and clinical technologies. Work Remotely - No Work Location: Buffalo, NY Job Type: Full Time, Exempt Pay: $100,000.00 - $120,000.00 Annually Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Faculty rank will be commensurate with education and qualifications. About D'Youville University: Shaping the Future of Education at D'Youville University D’Youville University, a nationally ranked private university in Buffalo, New York, is transforming lives through a unique blend of academics and holistic development. Committed to promoting a health mind, body, and spirit, D’Youville empowers individuals to realize their potential, thrive in their careers, and make meaningful contributions to society. A Dynamic and Purpose-Driven Community Located on Buffalo’s vibrant West Side, just blocks from a bustling downtown, D’Youville University is deeply embedded in an energetic, diverse urban landscape. Under the visionary leadership of President Lorrie Clemo, the university is undergoing an exciting evolution, with innovative initiatives designed to meet societal needs, elevate student experiences, expand career readiness, and solidify our role as a leader in 21st-century education. A Place for Growth and Innovation D’Youville University offers education across health sciences and business, with a range of degree levels, advanced certificates, accelerated paths, and community-engaged learning experiences. Our dedication to preparing students for successful careers is showcased in our national ranking for social mobility making us the top private university in the City of Buffalo. Why Work with Us? As a D’Youville University Saint, you’ll be joining a collaborative, innovation-driven community committed to academic excellence, social responsibility, and transformative growth. When you join our team, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a university making a real difference—for our students, our community, and our world. Explore the possibilities at dyu.edu . All job offers are contingent upon legal authorization to work in New York State as determined by the NYS Department of Labor. Apply for this position Get Updates Are you interested in hearing about new opportunities at D'Youville University? Enter your email address to get a weekly email when new positions are posted. send Powered by HiringThing © 2026\n\t\t\t\t| Privacy Policy Admin Login | Subscribe via RSS"
