    "https://dyouville-university.prismhr-hire.com/job/1047929/center-for-workforce-development-adjunct-instructor": {
      "title": "Center for Workforce Development - Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Center for Workforce Development - Adjunct Instructor @ D'Youville University Share: Center for Workforce Development - Adjunct Instructor Buffalo, NY D’Youville University is seeking Workforce Development Adjunct Instructors to support short-term healthcare and allied health training programs. These positions are course-based and scheduled as workforce programs are offered. Adjunct instructors will be scheduled based on program needs, course schedules, enrollment, and instructor qualifications. This is an adjunct, course-based role. Assignments will vary depending on course offerings and enrollment. Some responsibilities may be completed remotely, including online course oversight and student communication. Skills labs, demonstrations, simulations, and competency assessments will be conducted in person at D’Youville or another approved training location. The ideal candidate is a strong practitioner who enjoys teaching, mentoring, and helping students prepare for meaningful entry-level healthcare careers. Responsibilities: Teach or support      short-term workforce courses in online, hybrid, and/or in-person formats. Monitor student progress      in online course materials, assignments, and required modules as      assigned. Respond to student      questions during the course and help students stay on track. Lead      or assist with in-person skills labs, demonstrations,      simulations, practice sessions, and competency checkoffs. Provide coaching,      feedback, and remediation to students as needed. Reinforce safety,      professionalism, communication, attendance expectations, and workplace      readiness. Maintain accurate attendance,      skills, grading, and student progress documentation. Work collaboratively      with the Director of Workforce Development, Skills Supervisor, program      leads, and employer partners. Follow D’Youville      policies and applicable program, certification, regulatory, safety, and      documentation requirements. Potential Program Areas: Adjunct instructors may support one or more workforce programs depending on their background, qualifications, and program needs, including: Certified Nursing      Assistant Phlebotomy Technician EKG Technician Sterile Processing      Technician Community Health Worker Medical Assistant Pharmacy Technician Behavioral Health      Technician Patient care and allied      health skills Other entry-level      healthcare workforce programs as developed Some programs may require specific credentials, licensure, certification, or field experience. Qualifications: Required: Professional experience      in healthcare, allied health, clinical practice, workforce training,      or a related field. Ability to      teach, demonstrate, coach, and evaluate entry-level healthcare or      allied health skills. Strong communication,      organization, and student support skills. Comfort working with      adult learners and students entering healthcare for the first time. Ability to use online      learning platforms and basic instructional technology. Commitment to student      success, workforce development, and professional standards. Ability to meet      program-specific qualifications, certification requirements, and      institutional requirements. Preferred: Prior teaching,      precepting, training, mentoring, staff development, or clinical education      experience. Relevant license,      certification, or credential in the program area being taught. Experience with skills      labs, simulations, competency checkoffs, or workplace training. Experience supporting      hybrid or online learning. Flexibility to support      evening, weekend, or accelerated course schedules. Work Remotely - Partial Work Location: Buffalo, NY Job Type: Adjunct About D'Youville University: Shaping the Future of Education at D'Youville University D’Youville University, a nationally ranked private university in Buffalo, New York, is transforming lives through a unique blend of academics and holistic development. Committed to promoting a health mind, body, and spirit, D’Youville empowers individuals to realize their potential, thrive in their careers, and make meaningful contributions to society. A Dynamic and Purpose-Driven Community Located on Buffalo’s vibrant West Side, just blocks from a bustling downtown, D’Youville University is deeply embedded in an energetic, diverse urban landscape. Under the visionary leadership of President Lorrie Clemo, the university is undergoing an exciting evolution, with innovative initiatives designed to meet societal needs, elevate student experiences, expand career readiness, and solidify our role as a leader in 21st-century education. A Place for Growth and Innovation D’Youville University offers education across health sciences and business, with a range of degree levels, advanced certificates, accelerated paths, and community-engaged learning experiences. Our dedication to preparing students for successful careers is showcased in our national ranking for social mobility making us the top private university in the City of Buffalo. Why Work with Us? As a D’Youville University Saint, you’ll be joining a collaborative, innovation-driven community committed to academic excellence, social responsibility, and transformative growth. When you join our team, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a university making a real difference—for our students, our community, and our world. Explore the possibilities at dyu.edu . All job offers are contingent upon legal authorization to work in New York State as determined by the NYS Department of Labor. Get Updates Are you interested in hearing about new opportunities at D'Youville University? Enter your email address to get a weekly email when new positions are posted. Powered by HiringThing © 2026\n\t\t\t\t| Privacy Policy Admin Login | Subscribe via RSS"
